---
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import Container from "../components/Container.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="AI & Workers — Syntila"
  description="Connect ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, coding agents, and local models to your Syntila Spaces. Workers run on your own computer with the AI tools you already use."
>
  <Section>
    <Container>
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="AI & Workers"
        title="Connect and share your favorite AI models."
        description="A Worker is an AI tool on your computer that a Space is allowed to use. Install and sign in to the tool, then ask it to work on your project from the web or mobile. Your connected computer must be awake and online."
        headingLevel={1}
      />

      <div class="cards worker-catalog worker-catalog--visual" data-site-event="section.workers_reached">
        <article class="worker-card">
          <div class="worker-card__top">
            <div class="worker-card__mark" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/icons/workers/chatgpt.png" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <h2>ChatGPT</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Runs through OpenAI's Codex CLI. Good for reasoning, writing, summaries, and code.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="worker-card">
          <div class="worker-card__top">
            <div class="worker-card__mark" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/icons/workers/claude.png" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <h2>Claude</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Runs through Anthropic's Claude Code. Good for long documents, planning, code changes, and review.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="worker-card">
          <div class="worker-card__top">
            <div class="worker-card__mark" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/icons/workers/copilot-dark.png" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <h2>Copilot</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Repository-aware help and terminal tasks through GitHub Copilot's command-line agent.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="worker-card">
          <div class="worker-card__top">
            <div class="worker-card__mark" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/icons/workers/gemini.png" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <h2>Gemini</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Runs through Google's Antigravity CLI. Good for fast research, large inputs, and a second point of view.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="worker-card">
          <div class="worker-card__top">
            <div class="worker-card__mark" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/icons/workers/grok-dark.png" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <h2>Grok</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Reasoning and coding tasks through xAI's Grok Build command-line agent.</p>
        </article>

        <article class="worker-card">
          <div class="worker-card__top">
            <div class="worker-card__mark" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/icons/workers/mcp.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" /></div>
            <h2>MCP</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Connect a local model, such as one served by Ollama, or your own agent as a Worker over the Model Context Protocol (MCP).</p>
        </article>
      </div>



      <div class="security-callout section-block-gap-lg" id="sharing">
        <strong>Check your plan before you share a Worker.</strong>
        <span>Your provider’s terms determine whether others can use a Worker you connect. Check your plan before sharing; personal subscriptions may be limited to one person. <a href="/faq/#sharing-subscriptions">Read more in the FAQ</a>.</span>
      </div>

      <div class="section-block-gap-lg">
        <SectionHeader
          eyebrow="MCP Servers &amp; Tools"
          title="Give Workers extra tools with MCP servers."
          description="Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers add tools, such as a database or an issue tracker, that a Worker can call. You register them on your own computer and approve what they offer before any Worker can use them."
        />
        <div class="execution-path-strip mcp-flow">
          <div class="execution-path-step"><div class="mcp-flow__heading"><div class="mcp-flow__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><rect x="7" y="9" width="34" height="30" rx="4"/><path d="M24 16v16m-8-8h16"/></svg></div>
            <span>Register</span></div>
            <strong>Add local or remote servers</strong>
            <p>Use <code>syntila mcp add</code> for a server on your computer or <code>syntila mcp add-remote</code> for one reached over HTTPS.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="execution-path-step"><div class="mcp-flow__heading"><div class="mcp-flow__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><path d="M24 6 38 12v10c0 9-5 15-14 20-9-5-14-11-14-20V12L24 6Z"/><path d="m17 24 5 5 9-10"/></svg></div>
            <span>Approve</span></div>
            <strong>Review each tool once</strong>
            <p>Syntila records exactly what each tool says it does. If a server later changes a tool, calls are blocked until you review it again.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="execution-path-step"><div class="mcp-flow__heading"><div class="mcp-flow__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><rect x="6" y="9" width="36" height="26" rx="3"/><path d="M18 40h12m-6-5v5M13 18h22m-22 7h14"/></svg></div>
            <span>Keep it local</span></div>
            <strong>Separate settings per run</strong>
            <p>Each run gets its own temporary MCP settings. Your normal CLI configuration is not changed, and server tokens stay on your computer.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="execution-path-step"><div class="mcp-flow__heading"><div class="mcp-flow__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><circle cx="24" cy="24" r="17"/><path d="m21 16 12 8-12 8V16Z"/></svg></div>
            <span>Run</span></div>
            <strong>Under your account</strong>
            <p>Approved servers run as you, on your computer, with output size limits and cleanup when the run ends.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="actions actions--center section-block-gap-lg">
        <Button href="https://app.syntila.app" label="Open Syntila" event="cta.open_app" />
        <Button href="/downloads/" label="Download Syntila Workspace" variant="secondary" event="navigation.downloads" />
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>
</SiteLayout>
